nodecode-acedatacloud-media is a rewrite of AceDataCloud's AceDataCloud/AceDataCloudMediaHermes:
https://github.com/AceDataCloud/AceDataCloudMediaHermes
commit 8eaebfb86152d754061375de881548bfa096dd2d
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ace Data Cloud (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's one HTTP client against api.acedata.cloud and the seventeen
service descriptions it carries, in Common Lisp. The service names, their generate and task
paths, the defaults each service fills in (model, size, ratio, resolution, duration, count,
audio and instrumental flags), the fields a call may set on each, the submit-then-retrieve task
flow with its bounded sixty-second poll, the finished_at/success/state reading of an answer, the
allowlist of fields an answer keeps, the bearer key on every request, and the statement that a
call spends Ace Data Cloud credits without an approval prompt all follow the original. The
Hermes toolset registry, the per-service enable/disable switch, and the Nano Banana
image_generate provider lane are what the rewrite leaves out: a Nodecode cell registers its own
tools, its own command and its own config section, so the seventeen per-service toolsets became
five tools that name their service, a /media command, and one generic task tool. Google Search
and face analysis keep their two endpoints, folded into one lookup tool. Nothing of the original
code is bundled; the rewrite is Lisp, and speaks the same HTTP API.
